Conflicts: aims-os-centre-senegal-labo
Description: AIMS OS — AIMS Senegal lab software on a personal computer
 Installs on a personal AIMS OS computer, a student's laptop for
 instance, the software of the AIMS Senegal (Mbour) lab workstations:
 every AIMS OS layer, virtual machines, Podman, and through a background
 service the vendor tools of the lab (RStudio, VS Code, Chrome, Zotero,
 Zoom, JupyterLab, Anaconda, Julia, SageMath, Android Studio, TeX Live,
 DBeaver, GNS3, Packet Tracer and more).
 .
 Unlike aims-os-centre-senegal-labo, it does not lock local accounts,
 open remote access for the IT team or join the campus directory. The
 installer and the weekly update come from the latest published lab
 package, so a personal computer gets the same versions as the lab.
 .
 The first pass downloads about 40 GB and takes several hours; it starts
 right after installation and resumes the next day if it was cut short.
 Nothing is downloaded on a metered connection. Packet Tracer and the
 virtual machine images come once the computer is on the campus network.
